What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/89600000.sipa-dele/cp_session
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        UDX710 AP-side port maintainers
Description:
                Read-only ASCII line:
                "1 dst channel generation connected restart_blocked error\n".
                The first six fields are decimal u32; error is signed decimal
                errno (zero or negative). dst/channel identify the selected CP
                delegator (UDX710 PSCP dst5, SIPA channel120). The software epoch,
                connected and restart_blocked fields are sampled under the
                existing delegator lock, with the sticky atomic error sampled
                within that interval. No transport messages or MMIO are read.
                connected reports the AP control-channel state, not a hardware
                grant or network-ready result. restart_blocked or nonzero error
                requires stopping dependent user processes and the documented
                cold-machine recovery, without attempting CP-only restart.
                Before the first connected observation, generation can change
                during initial handshake. After a baseline is armed, a changed
                generation or lost connection invalidates the observed session.
                The sysfs file disappears on provider removal; this is an error,
                never a reset-to-zero or newly authenticated session.
